# Krystal Loop Protocol Licensing

Free for individuals and small businesses. Larger organisations can evaluate
it freely and need a commercial licence to use it in their work.

This repository uses separate licences for software and documentation.

## Software

Source code, scripts, configuration examples, schemas, and tests are licensed
under the PolyForm Small Business License 1.0.0. See
`LICENSE-PolyForm-Small-Business-1.0.0`.

Required Notice: Copyright Krystal Unity (https://krystalunity.com)

In short: your company may use, change and share the software at no charge if
it has fewer than 100 people working for it and had less than 1,000,000 USD
(2019, adjusted for inflation) revenue in the prior tax year. The licence text
governs.

### Additional Permissions

For an individual or an organisation of any size, each of these is also a
permitted purpose under that licence:

- personal use that is not for the benefit of a company;
- evaluating the software, including verifying and rerunning the published
  benchmarks, but not using it for production work;
- teaching and non-commercial research.

### Commercial Licences

Organisations above the small-business limits can license the software for
their work. Write to sales@krystalunity.com.

### Earlier Versions

Revisions of this repository up to and including commit `d225053`
(2 November 2026) were published under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and
remain available under that licence.

## Documentation

Prose documentation, including Markdown files in the repository root and under
`docs/`, `adapters/`, and `examples/`, is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence. See `LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0`.
Recommended attribution: "Krystal Loop Protocol by Krystal Unity," with a
link to the original repository and an indication of changes where applicable.

Files carrying an explicit licence notice are governed by that notice.
